    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the stability concerns, but the DEP design philosophy assumes that a distributed system is inherently more resilient to the exact kind of surges you're worried about. The goal is to move away from having one \"brain\" that can be targeted. If the local switches have the necessary response time, the aggregate stability should hold. Can you go deeper into what specific scenarios you think the local switches would fail to handle compared to your current active management?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
