      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the distributed design improves resilience against cyber attacks, local switches would likely struggle with coordinating complex, non-linear cascading failures that require instantaneous, global-wide recalculations. They may also lack the coordinated memory of recent aggregate trends needed to make optimal prognostic decisions across the entire grid simultaneously. Given this, the temporary dip in predictive accuracy during these specific cascading events is the primary risk I foresee in the transition.",
      "source": "target",
